Article 14

1. Prevention of the occurrence of acts of violence against women and children as referred to in Article 13, shall be carried out….

D:\PERDA PDF\2-PERDA PERLINDUNGAN HAK PEREMPUAN DAN ANAK.doc 10 carried out by OPD and UKPD whose duties and functions are in the fields of:
a. social affairs;
b. health;
c. education;
d. manpower;
e. women's empowerment and child protection;
f. youth and sports;
g. population and civil registration;
h. mental and spiritual; andi. peace and order.
2. Prevention of acts of violence by OPD and UKPD as referred to in paragraph (1), shall be carried out in an integrated and continuous manner based on the Regional Action Plan.
3. In addition to the Regional Government, prevention as referred to in paragraph (1) must be carried out by:a. family and/or closest relatives;
b. society;
c. educational institutions;
d. health institutions;
e. social community institutions; andf. business world and other institutions.

CHAPTER III

PRINCIPLES AND OBJECTIVES

Article 3

Protection of women and children from acts of violence and discrimination shall be conducted based on the principles of:
a. respect for human rights;
b. justice and gender equality;
c. non-discrimination;
d. protection of victims;
e. empowerment; andf. integration.

Article 28

1. In order to achieve the objectives of protection of women and children from acts of violence as referred to in Article 3, the Regional Government cooperates with:a. the Government;
b. the Provincial Government;
c. other Regency/City Governments; andd. non-governmental institutions.
2. Cooperation as referred to in paragraph (1), includes: a. provision of data and information;
b. rehabilitation of victims of acts of violence;
c. repatriation and social reintegration; andd. provision of evidence and witnesses;
3. Cooperation as referred to in paragraph (1) and paragraph (2) shall be implemented in accordance with the provisions of laws and regulations.

CHAPTER VIII

SPECIAL PROTECTION OF CHILDREN

Article 15

1. Special protection of children is provided to:a. children in emergency situations;
b. children in conflict with the law;
c. children from minority and isolated groups;
d. children who are exploited economically and/or sexually; e. children who are victims of narcotics abuse,  alcohol, psychotropic substances, and other addictive substances;
f. children who are victims of pornography;
g. children with HIV/AIDS;
h. children….

D:\PERDA PDF\2-PERDA PERLINDUNGAN HAK PEREMPUAN DAN ANAK.doc 11
h. children victims of kidnapping, sale, and/or  trafficking;
i. children victims of physical and/or psychological violence;
j. children victims of sexual crimes;
k. children victims of terrorist networks;
l. children with disabilities;
m. children victims of abuse and neglect;
n. children with deviant social behavior; ando. children who are victims of stigmatization from labeling  related to their parents' condition.
2. The Regional Government in implementing the handling  of special protection of children as referred to  in paragraph (1) shall be in accordance with the provisions of laws and regulations.

CHAPTER II

SCOPE

Article 2

The scope of protection of women and children from acts of violence, is as follows:
a. principles and objectives;
b. forms of violence;
c. rights of women and children victims of violence;
d. obligations and responsibilities;
e. prevention of acts of violence;
f. special protection of children;
g. service and empowerment of victims of acts of violence;
h. institutions;
i. cooperation and partnership;
j. reporting;
k. guidance….

D:\PERDA PDF\2-PERDA PERLINDUNGAN HAK PEREMPUAN DAN ANAK.doc 5
k. guidance and supervision; and
l. financing.

Article 12

Every person who hears, sees, or knows of the occurrence of violence against women and children is obliged to make efforts in accordance with their capacity to:  a. prevent and stop the continuation of acts of violence;
b. provide protection to victims;
d. provide….

D:\PERDA PDF\2-PERDA PERLINDUNGAN HAK PEREMPUAN DAN ANAK.doc 9
d. provide emergency assistance; and/ore. assist in the process of filing an application for protection order.

CHAPTER XIII

GUIDANCE AND SUPERVISION

Article 31

1. The Regional Government is obliged to conduct guidance and supervision of the provision of protection for women and children from acts of violence.
2. Guidance as referred to in paragraph (1), includes: a. guidelines and fulfillment standards;
b. technical guidance and training;
c. provision of facilities;
d. monitoring; ande. evaluation.
3. Guidance….

D:\PERDA PDF\2-PERDA PERLINDUNGAN HAK PEREMPUAN DAN ANAK.doc 18 (3) Guidance as referred to in paragraph (2), is in order to realize the objectives of protection of the rights of women and children from acts of violence in accordance with minimum service standards implemented by related OPD/agencies and the community.

CHAPTER V

RIGHTS OF WOMEN AND CHILDREN VICTIMS OF ACTS OF VIOLENCE

Article 6

Women and children victims of acts of violence shall receive the following rights:
a. the right to have their dignity respected as human beings; b. the right to recovery of health and psychological recovery from the suffering experienced by victims;
c. the right to determine their own decisions;
d. the right to obtain information;
e. the right to confidentiality;
f. the right to compensation;
g. the right to social rehabilitation;
h. the right to complaint handling;
i. the right of victims and their families to obtain facilities in the judicial process; andj. the right to assistance.

Article 17

1. Forms of services provided to women and  children victims of violence are as follows: a. complaint services;
b. health services;
c. assistance….

D:\PERDA PDF\2-PERDA PERLINDUNGAN HAK PEREMPUAN DAN ANAK.doc 12
c. legal assistance;
d. social rehabilitation and reintegration;
e. repatriation;
f. identification services; andg. psychological services.
2. Services as referred to in paragraph (1) must  be supported by facilities in the form of:a. special service rooms in police lines;
b. expert and professional personnel;
c. service centers and safe houses; and/ord. other facilities and infrastructure needed for  victim recovery.
3. Forms of services as referred to in paragraph (1),  are implemented in accordance with minimum service standards  established by the government and implemented by related OPDs  whose duties and functions are in the fields of:a. social affairs;
b. health;
c. women's empowerment and child protection; and d. mental and spiritual.
4. In carrying out the duties and functions as referred to  in paragraph (1), the Regional Government cooperates with  government agencies, other regional governments, non-governmental organizations, and social institutions.
5. Further provisions regarding the procedures for services  for handling women and children from violence  as referred to in paragraph (1), paragraph (2) and paragraph (3),  shall be regulated by Regent Regulation.

